<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stjepan Radić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871–1928</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stjepan Radić was a Croatian politician who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-peasant-party">Croatian Peasant Party</a> with his brother Antun in 1904 and led the Croat opposition to Serbian centralism in the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>. Imprisoned in 1925, he then briefly joined the government. In June 1928 a Montenegrin deputy shot him in the parliament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, and his death in August led King Alexander to impose a royal dictatorship in 1929.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stjepan-radic.jpg" alt="Stjepan Radić" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stjepan-Radic.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
